{"term":"argument","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:dbf6ef0a3c4a73c4a3","definition":"A fact or statement used to support a proposition; a reason.","example":"There is no greater, at leaſt no more palpable and convincing Argument of the Exiſtence of a Deity than the admirable Art and Wiſdom that diſcovers itſelf in the make and conſtitution, the order and diſpoſition, the ends and uſes of all the parts and members of this ſtately fabrick of Heaven and Earth.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["argument","assertion","basis","claim","contention","proof"],"antonyms":["recantation"],"collocations":[],"usage":"also, figuratively","register":"also, countable, figuratively","wordFamily":["argumentable","argumental","argumentary","argumentation","argumentative","argumentatively","argumentativeness","argument form","argument-form","argument from design","argument from ignorance","argument from illusion","argument from silence","argumenthood","argument instance","argumentive","argumentize","argumentless","argument mining","multiargument","sargable","an argument"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/argument#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:dfcca5690d040f302d","definition":"A process of reasoning; argumentation.","example":"Indeed, I cannot commend my life; for I am conſcious to my ſelf of many failings: therein, I know alſo that a man by his converſation, may ſoon overthrow what by argument or perſwaſion he doth labour to faſten upon others for their good: […]","pos":"noun","synonyms":["argument","assertion","basis","claim","contention","proof"],"antonyms":["recantation"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable","wordFamily":["argumentable","argumental","argumentary","argumentation","argumentative","argumentatively","argumentativeness","argument form","argument-form","argument from design","argument from ignorance","argument from illusion","argument from silence","argumenthood","argument instance","argumentive","argumentize","argumentless","argument mining","multiargument","sargable","an argument"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/argument#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ea873fd291542c5428","definition":"An abstract or summary of the content of a literary work such as a book, a poem or a major section such as a chapter, included in the work before the content itself; (figuratively) the contents themselves.","example":"If I would broach the veſſels of my loue, / And try the argument of hearts, by borrowing, / Men, and mens fortunes, could I frankely vſe / As I can bid thee ſpeake.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["argument","assertion","basis","claim","contention","proof"],"antonyms":["recantation"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable","wordFamily":["argumentable","argumental","argumentary","argumentation","argumentative","argumentatively","argumentativeness","argument form","argument-form","argument from design","argument from ignorance","argument from illusion","argument from silence","argumenthood","argument instance","argumentive","argumentize","argumentless","argument mining","multiargument","sargable","an argument"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/argument#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:4c0d1b1e93e27e9445","definition":"A verbal dispute; a quarrel.","example":"The neighbours got into an argument about the branches of the trees that extended over the fence.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["argument","argy-bargy","altercation","contention","barney","bawl out","blue","bobbery","brawl","clash","conflict","controversy","debate","difference","ding-dong","disagreement","discordance","disharmony","disputation","dispute","dissonance","disunion","dustup","face-off","falling out","feud","fight","flite","hassle","issue","palaver","quarrel","quibble","row","spat","squabble","tangle","threap","tiff","wrangle"],"antonyms":["recantation"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable","wordFamily":["argumentable","argumental","argumentary","argumentation","argumentative","argumentatively","argumentativeness","argument form","argument-form","argument from design","argument from ignorance","argument from illusion","argument from silence","argumenthood","argument instance","argumentive","argumentize","argumentless","argument mining","multiargument","sargable","an argument"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/argument#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:bc0ebbfd8cbcef4289","definition":"Any dispute, altercation, or collision.","example":"Steve got in a physical argument with his neighbor and came away with a black eye.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["argument","assertion","basis","claim","contention","proof"],"antonyms":["recantation"],"collocations":[],"usage":"broadly, euphemistic, humorous","register":"broadly, countable, euphemistic, humorous, uncountable","wordFamily":["argumentable","argumental","argumentary","argumentation","argumentative","argumentatively","argumentativeness","argument form","argument-form","argument from design","argument from ignorance","argument from illusion","argument from silence","argumenthood","argument instance","argumentive","argumentize","argumentless","argument mining","multiargument","sargable","an argument"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/argument#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:f3367342ba1a22724b","definition":"Any of the phrases that bear a syntactic connection to the verb of a clause.","example":"In numerous works over the past two decades, beginning with the pioneering work of Gruber (1965), Fillmore (1968a), and Jackendoff (1972), it has been argued that each Argument (i.e. Subject or Complement) of a Predicate bears a particular thematic role (alias theta-role, or θ-role to its Predicate), and that the set of thematic functions which Arguments can fulfil are drawn from a highly restricted, finite, universal set.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["argument","assertion","basis","claim","contention","proof"],"antonyms":["recantation"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable","wordFamily":["argumentable","argumental","argumentary","argumentation","argumentative","argumentatively","argumentativeness","argument form","argument-form","argument from design","argument from ignorance","argument from illusion","argument from silence","argumenthood","argument instance","argumentive","argumentize","argumentless","argument mining","multiargument","sargable","an argument"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/argument#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c1461768097de6c955","definition":"The independent variable of a function.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":["argument","assertion","basis","claim","contention","proof"],"antonyms":["recantation"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["argumentable","argumental","argumentary","argumentation","argumentative","argumentatively","argumentativeness","argument form","argument-form","argument from design","argument from ignorance","argument from illusion","argument from silence","argumenthood","argument instance","argumentive","argumentize","argumentless","argument mining","multiargument","sargable","an argument"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/argument#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:64e6aa76b89227c5b4","definition":"The phase of a complex number.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":["argument","assertion","basis","claim","contention","proof"],"antonyms":["recantation"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["argumentable","argumental","argumentary","argumentation","argumentative","argumentatively","argumentativeness","argument form","argument-form","argument from design","argument from ignorance","argument from illusion","argument from silence","argumenthood","argument instance","argumentive","argumentize","argumentless","argument mining","multiargument","sargable","an argument"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/argument#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:1266ecc20b39a7eedd","definition":"A quantity on which the calculation of another quantity depends.","example":"The altitude is the argument of the refraction.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["argument","assertion","basis","claim","contention","proof"],"antonyms":["recantation"],"collocations":[],"usage":"also","register":"also, countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["argumentable","argumental","argumentary","argumentation","argumentative","argumentatively","argumentativeness","argument form","argument-form","argument from design","argument from ignorance","argument from illusion","argument from silence","argumenthood","argument instance","argumentive","argumentize","argumentless","argument mining","multiargument","sargable","an argument"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/argument#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:f93b5621c19fd32c13","definition":"A value, or a reference to a value, passed to a function.","example":"Parameters are like labelled fillable blanks used to define a function whereas arguments are passed to a function when calling it, filling in those blanks.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["actual argument","passed parameter"],"antonyms":["recantation"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["argumentable","argumental","argumentary","argumentation","argumentative","argumentatively","argumentativeness","argument form","argument-form","argument from design","argument from ignorance","argument from illusion","argument from silence","argumenthood","argument instance","argumentive","argumentize","argumentless","argument mining","multiargument","sargable","an argument"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/argument#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:6fa94abfd6e2628a8c","definition":"A parameter at a function call; an actual parameter, as opposed to a formal parameter.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":["argument","assertion","basis","claim","contention","proof"],"antonyms":["recantation"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["argumentable","argumental","argumentary","argumentation","argumentative","argumentatively","argumentativeness","argument form","argument-form","argument from design","argument from ignorance","argument from illusion","argument from silence","argumenthood","argument instance","argumentive","argumentize","argumentless","argument mining","multiargument","sargable","an argument"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/argument#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:fe3caedc19f28fe143","definition":"A matter in question; a business in hand.","example":"As neere as I could ſift him on that argument,\n On ſome apparent danger ſeene in him,\n Aimde at your highnes, no inueterate malice.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["argument","assertion","basis","claim","contention","proof"],"antonyms":["recantation"],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"countable, obsolete, uncountable","wordFamily":["argumentable","argumental","argumentary","argumentation","argumentative","argumentatively","argumentativeness","argument form","argument-form","argument from design","argument from ignorance","argument from illusion","argument from silence","argumenthood","argument instance","argumentive","argumentize","argumentless","argument mining","multiargument","sargable","an argument"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/argument#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:84b7d53e6a1345e85a","definition":"The subject matter of an artistic representation, discourse, or writing; a theme or topic.","example":"[I]n vttering the ſtuffe ye receiued of the one, in declaring the order ye tooke with the other, ye ſhall neuer lacke, neither matter, nor maner, what to write, nor how to write in this kinde of Argument.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["argument","assertion","basis","claim","contention","proof"],"antonyms":["recantation"],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"countable, obsolete, uncountable","wordFamily":["argumentable","argumental","argumentary","argumentation","argumentative","argumentatively","argumentativeness","argument form","argument-form","argument from design","argument from ignorance","argument from illusion","argument from silence","argumenthood","argument instance","argumentive","argumentize","argumentless","argument mining","multiargument","sargable","an argument"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/argument#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c2fb7df652dcb17bc3","definition":"Evidence, proof; (countable) an item of such evidence or proof.","example":"[F]or louing me, by my troth it is no addition to her wit, nor no great argument of her follie, for I will be horribly in loue with her, […]","pos":"noun","synonyms":["argument","assertion","basis","claim","contention","proof"],"antonyms":["recantation"],"collocations":[],"usage":"archaic","register":"archaic, uncountable","wordFamily":["argumentable","argumental","argumentary","argumentation","argumentative","argumentatively","argumentativeness","argument form","argument-form","argument from design","argument from ignorance","argument from illusion","argument from silence","argumenthood","argument instance","argumentive","argumentize","argumentless","argument mining","multiargument","sargable","an argument"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/argument#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:306cf15dc84c04a787","definition":"To put forward as an argument; to argue.","example":"[I]t is moſt certaine, that after Herodotus and other auncient writers, it is ſafer to call theſe [elephants' tusks] teeth, then hornes; and I will breefly ſet downe the reaſons of Philoſtratus, that will haue them to be teeth, and afterward of Grapaldus [i.e., Francesco Mario Grapaldi], Aelianus, and Pauſanias, that would make them horns, and ſo leaue the reader to conſider whether opinion he thinketh moſt agreeable to truth. […] Thus they argument for the horns of Elephants.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"nonstandard, obsolete","register":"intransitive, nonstandard, obsolete","wordFamily":["argumentable","argumental","argumentary","argumentation","argumentative","argumentatively","argumentativeness","argument form","argument-form","argument from design","argument from ignorance","argument from illusion","argument from silence","argumenthood","argument instance","argumentive","argumentize","argumentless","argument mining","multiargument","sargable","an argument"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/argument#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d5436a0bc33a7df4ca","definition":"To adduce evidence, to provide proof.","example":"Albeit that it apperteneth to the apoſtolis, be the puiſtoun of God to tak ordour in all materis off debait cõcernyng ye faith, & ſpecialie to iterprete ye ſcripturis, as yat quhilkis had yͤ ſpreit of god, & wer yͤ trew kirk: It argumẽtis [argumentis] not yat vtheris, quha hes ꝯuenit [conuenit] ſenſyne in generale ꝯſales [consales] had the ſpreit of GOD, or wer the trew kirk: […]","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"intransitive, obsolete","wordFamily":["argumentable","argumental","argumentary","argumentation","argumentative","argumentatively","argumentativeness","argument form","argument-form","argument from design","argument from ignorance","argument from illusion","argument from silence","argumenthood","argument instance","argumentive","argumentize","argumentless","argument mining","multiargument","sargable","an argument"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/argument#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"}],"pronunciation":{"ipa":"/ˈɑːɡjʊmənt/","us":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/3/30/En-us-argument.ogg/En-us-argument.ogg.mp3"},"wordFamily":["argumentable","argumental","argumentary","argumentation","argumentative","argumentatively","argumentativeness","argument form","argument-form","argument from design","argument from ignorance","argument from illusion","argument from silence","argumenthood","argument instance","argumentive","argumentize","argumentless","argument mining","multiargument","sargable","an argument"]}